- The timeit module uses `timeit.default_timer` which on CPython is `time.perf_counter()`. So they should be using the same timer!
- Wait, let me check: timeit.repeat() with number=1 should give essentially the same timer as direct perf_counter calls.
- The difference might be due to the lambda overhead in timeit, which would make timeit give HIGHER times, not lower.
